    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>It was mentioned that the reasoning for this change was absent from this ticket. So I will add my interpretation for context.</p>\n\n<p>Currently Fedora 6 is storing triples for binary resources using the binary description’s ID.</p>\n\n<p>i.e. BINARY_RESOURCE/fcr:metadata instead of just BINARY_RESOURCE</p>\n\n<p>The migration code made the opposite assumption, which led to users having difficulty removing triples (mostly because when displayed the BINARY_RESOURCE/fcr:metadata subject was changed to BINARY_RESOURCE). This led to a discussion about the reasoning for storing the triples one way but displaying them the alternate way.</p>\n\n<p>It made more sense that the triples were stored in OCFL as Fedora was displaying them for long-term stability. </p>",
     "created": "03/May/22 1:31 PM",
     "id": "22630",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/13722/comment/22630",
     "updateAuthor": {
